  "description": "Official Ukrainian system for names in passports and for geographic names (Cabinet of Ministers Resolution No. 55 of 27.01.2010; also BGN/PCGN 2019 and UNGEGN): Г→H, Ґ→G, И→Y, І→I; Є Ї Й Ю Я → YE YI Y YU YA at word start, IE I I IU IA elsewhere; ЗГ→ZGH; Ь and apostrophe are not rendered.",
  "sources": [
    "https://zakon.rada.gov.ua/laws/show/55-2010-%D0%BF",
    "https://geonames.nga.mil/geonames/GNSSearch/GNSDocs/romanization/ROMANIZATION_OF_UKRAINIAN.pdf",
    "https://zakon.rada.gov.ua/laws/show/152-2014-%D0%BF",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanization_of_Ukrainian"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "All official examples from the resolution are included as samples.",
    "A letter after an apostrophe is not word-initial (Короп'є → Koropie, Мар'їне → Marine, Знам'янка → Znamianka); each part of a hyphenated name is a separate word (Анна-Яна → Anna-Yana).",
    "Passports follow this table by default, but on written request the Latin spelling may follow earlier Ukrainian documents, legalized foreign civil-status documents or a relative's passport (KMU Resolution No. 152 of 2014, para. 108).",
    "ICAO Doc 9303 Ukrainian rules coincide with this table except that ICAO has no ЗГ → ZGH rule."
  ],
